From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Ludovic Henry <git@ludovic.dev>
Date: Tue, 13 Oct 2026 00:00:00 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] lance-context-core: drop the unused lance-graph dependency

crates/lance-context-core/Cargo.toml depends on `lance-graph = "0.5.4"`,
but no Rust source file in this workspace imports `lance_graph`
(`grep -rln lance_graph crates/ python/` matches nothing); it is dead
weight in the dependency graph. lance-graph's own Cargo.toml pins
`lance`/`lance-core`/`lance-linalg` at an incompatible `1.x` line, which
Cargo resolves as yet another parallel copy of the whole lance-core/
lance-linalg family, alongside the `9.0.0` one crates/lance-context-core
depends on directly (`lance = "9.0.0"`) and the `7.0.0` one
`lancedb = "0.30.0"` still pulls in. That `1.x` copy's lance-core
SIMD_SUPPORT closure and lance-linalg's f32x8/f32x16/i32x8/f64x4/f64x8
SIMD types have no riscv64 fallback either, so it would need its own
riscv64-patched copy (see 0003-cargo-patch-lance-crates-for-riscv64.patch)
just to compile a crate nothing uses. Removing the dead dependency
drops that whole copy from resolution instead.

Upstream-Status: To upstream [not yet submitted to lance-format/lance-context]

Signed-off-by: Ludovic Henry <git@ludovic.dev>
---
diff --git a/crates/lance-context-core/Cargo.toml b/crates/lance-context-core/Cargo.toml
index a5d0f25..928c52a 100644
--- a/crates/lance-context-core/Cargo.toml
+++ b/crates/lance-context-core/Cargo.toml
@@ -31,7 +31,6 @@ lance-context-api = { version = "0.6.7", path = "../lance-context-api" }
 lance-index = "9.0.0"
 lance-namespace = "9.0.0"
 lancedb = "0.30.0"
-lance-graph = "0.5.4"
 # Version-matched with lance-context-server/-master so one process-wide recorder
 # serves every crate.
 metrics = { version = "0.24", optional = true }
-- 
2.43.0
